' Shared style + legend, included by every diagram in this folder.
' Convention used consistently across ALL bounded contexts and ALL layers:
'
'  1) Generalization (extends)            A --|> B   solid line, hollow triangle
'  2) Realization (implements), SAME      A ..|> B   dashed line, hollow triangle
'     container as the interface
'  3) Composition (owns, lifecycle-bound) A "1" *-- "0..*" B   filled diamond at owner
'  4) Aggregation (references, shared     A "1" o-- "0..*" B   hollow diamond at owner
'     lifecycle, e.g. many-to-many catalog entities)
'  5) Association (plain held field,      A --> B
'     same container)
'  6) Dependency, ANY relationship that   A ..> B : <<stereotype>>
'     CROSSES one of the drawn layer
'     containers (Domain / Application /
'     Infrastructure / Interfaces boxes)
'     -- per course guidance: a query/command
'     interface (domain) and its implementation
'     (application) are related by DEPENDENCY,
'     not realization, because they live in
'     different layer containers. The same rule
'     is generalized here to every cross-container
'     edge: repository ports implemented by
'     infrastructure adapters, outbound ports
'     implemented by infrastructure services,
'     ACL facades implemented across layers,
'     controllers using application services,
'     assemblers using domain commands/queries, etc.
'     Typical stereotypes used: <<implements>>,
'     <<uses>>, <<creates>>, <<publishes>>,
'     <<listens to>>, <<extends>>, <<converts>>.
'  7) Relationships to external framework types
'     (Spring Data, Spring Security, JJWT, etc.)
'     use the precise UML relation (generalization/
'     realization) against a small "«external»"
'     package, since these are not part of the
'     bounded context's own layering.
'
' Each layer diagram is self-contained: classes that belong to another layer
' but are referenced from the current one are drawn inside a clearly labeled
' "(referenced)" package so nothing is left floating without a relationship.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 6
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam class {
  BorderColor #6b7280
  ArrowColor #6b7280
  BackgroundColor #f8fafc
  FontSize 12
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #94a3b8
  FontStyle bold
  FontSize 13
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #fef9c3
  BorderColor #ca8a04
}
